From fecdea0221c7ef56008a8ed5911ef4ff222f99b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Velle Sinclair <brncomputerhelp@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 16:29:01 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 41/42] fix(scripting): engine.setTimeout and setInterval run,
 and cancel

The engine object was never put in the map its timer functions look
it up in. Only the destructor touched the map, so every setTimeout and
setInterval returned an exception that nothing had thrown and ended
the script as "[uninitialized]". 5 scripts in 2 wallpapers start
timers (Swimming Kirby's media panel, a vinyl's album cover that hides
a second after a track change).

With the map filled, three more faults would have followed:

  - The callback was kept without a reference of its own and then
    freed when the timer fired, a use-after-free.
  - The cancel function setTimeout returns read the timer id from its
    argument. Scripts call it bare (`stop ()`), so every cancel failed.
    It now reads the id it was made with.
  - The tick ran callbacks while iterating the timer maps, so a
    callback that cancelled a timer erased from a map under the loop.
    Due timers are now collected first and run by id. A timeout is
    gone before its callback runs, and an interval's callback is held
    while it runs.

A callback that throws is logged once instead of leaving its exception
pending for another script's error report to collect. A timer given
something other than a function is a TypeError.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TrYdVZ7ULsVD9WKX2Az4Mw
